## Splice point 5b: P/src/tests/CMakeLists.txt, beside the other per-pack-target
## census calls that follow hkp_verify_embedded_sources(). Add this call:
hkp_register_census_tests(TARGET hip_kernel_provider_tests
                          PACK_NAME product
                          SUITES Test{{ config.engine.pascal_name }}Packs
                          EXPECTED_CASES
{% for case in expected_cases %}
                              {{ case }}
{% endfor %}
                          )
##
## `PACK_NAME product` addresses the `product` pack target, wired only where the shipped
## root holds a descriptor AND at least one of them declares an architecture this build
## packs for. A build whose GPU_TARGETS your bundle does not declare leaves production
## packaging dormant: the call registers nothing and says so at STATUS, naming the
## dormant pack, so leave it unguarded. A PACK_NAME no pack target carries is a configure
## error, which is the typo this keeps visible.
##
## Commit your bundle under `E/descriptors/<producer>/<bundle>/` **before** splicing this
## call, or the census runs against a shard without your descriptors.
##
## The call registers one CTest entry per arch the `product` pack target was wired with:
## hip-kernel-provider-hkp-census-<arch>-Test{{ config.engine.pascal_name }}Packs,
## running hip_kernel_provider_tests --gtest_filter=Test{{ config.engine.pascal_name }}Packs.*
## with HIPDNN_TEST_CENSUS_SUITE=Test{{ config.engine.pascal_name }}Packs,
## HIPDNN_TEST_EXPECTED_ARCH=<arch> and HIPDNN_DESCRIPTOR_DIR set to that pack target's
## own out-root shard for <arch>, under the labels unit_test;hip-kernel-provider;host.
## Declare a suite name at one pack target only: the CTest name carries no pack
## component, so a second declaration is a configure error. Every registered case must
## execute and pass without skipping in every iteration; missing suites,
## filtered/disabled/sharded-out cases and zero iterations fail.
##
## EXPECTED_CASES is optional to configure and required for the census to mean what it
## claims, since the guard's obligations come from the cases the suite registered. The
## list above is read out of the suite this run rendered; re-splice whenever the bundle's
## shape changes.
